# Redirect map for the blog.risanb.com Gatsby -> Astro rewrite.
#
# Read by Cloudflare Workers static assets at deploy time (dist/_redirects), and
# parsed by scripts/check-site.mjs which fails the build if a rule would shadow a
# page the site actually serves.
#
# 301 is stated explicitly: the platform defaults to 302 when the status is left
# off, and a 302 does not carry ranking.
#
# ORDER: static rules first, then the single splat rule last, per Cloudflare's
# requirement that static redirects precede dynamic ones. The rules are disjoint
# so either order resolves identically today, but precedence is applied top-down
# and a future rule could quietly become unreachable.
#
# These redirects are applied by the static-assets layer. They are SKIPPED for
# any request a Worker script handles, which is why wrangler.jsonc deliberately
# defines no `main` script and no `run_worker_first`.
#
# Source: the 13 URLs in blog.risanb.com/sitemap.xml while Gatsby was live
# (2026-09-21 snapshot in scripts/legacy-urls.txt). Two shapes, both handled:
#
#   /photos/        -> /categories/photos/   (the old gallery is now a category)
#   /posts/<slug>/  -> /<slug>/              (11 URLs, one splat rule)
#
# The 142 posts served from risanb.com/blog/<slug>/ keep the same slug here, so
# risanb.com's own redirect file points them straight at /<slug>/ and needs no
# second hop.

# --- Gatsby-era photo gallery, now a category --------------------------------
/photos/  /categories/photos/  301

# --- Dropped posts ------------------------------------------------------------
/farewell/  /  301

# --- Gatsby-era post URLs ----------------------------------------------------
# Dynamic (splat) rule -- keep last, see ORDER note above.
/posts/*  /:splat  301
